    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10517": {
      "title": "Instructor of Education with a Reading Focus",
      "description": "Nicholls State University Portal | Instructor of Education with a Reading Focus Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Instructor of Education with a Reading Focus Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The anticipated start date for this position is January 13, 2027. Special Instructions Nicholls State University adheres to the equal opportunity provisions of federal civil rights laws and regulations that are applicable to this agency. Therefore, no one will be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, national origin (Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964); sex (Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972); disability (Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; or age (Age Discrimination Act of 1975) in attaining educational goals and objectives and in the administration of personnel policies and procedures. Anyone with questions regarding this policy may contact Alison Hadaway, SHRM -CP, Director of Human Resources at 985-448-4041 / alison.hadaway@nicholls.edu / P.O. Box 2105, Thibodaux, LA 70310. For anyone needing ADA Accommodations, please contact Carolyn Kern, Director of Environmental Health & Safety at 985-448-4782 / carolyn.kern@nicholls.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Instructor of Education with a Reading Focus Position Number 021425 Salary Range $49,415.00 Position Type Faculty Department Information Ending Effective Date of Temporary Employment Department Teacher Education Job Duties Responsibility / Duty U ndergraduate Instruction & Course Delivery: Teach undergraduate education courses (minimum 15 credit hours per semester), focusing primarily on early and elementary reading pedagogy grounded in the Science of Reading and Louisiana High-Quality Instructional Materials ( HQIM ) . Deliver additional foundational generalist courses as needed, such as Introduction to the Teaching Profession and Introduction to Special Education . Percentage Of Time 50 Responsibility / Duty Academic Advising & Candidate Retention: Serve as an undergraduate academic advisor, providing ongoing academic guidance, tracking degree progress, supporting candidate retention, and assisting with clinical/field placement coordination. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Accreditation, Assessment & State Compliance: Assist in data collection, reporting, and site visit preparation for state program reviews and specialized accreditation bodies ( LDOE , CAEP , TPI -US) to ensure alignment with state literacy mandates and competencies. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Departmental & Administrative Operations: Participate in departmental governance, attend faculty meetings, respond to administrative requests, and collaborate with departmental leadership to support program goals. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Student Consultation & Office Hours: Maintain scheduled, regular office hours to provide accessibility to candidates, offer instructional support, and collaborate with faculty colleagues. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty P–12 Collaboration & Professional Development: Engage in collaborative initiatives with local P–12 school partners and pursue continuous professional growth in elementary literacy research, pedagogy, and teacher education. Percentage Of Time 5 Responsibility / Duty Learning Environment & Engagement: Establish and maintain an inclusive, rigorous, and supportive learning environment conducive to candidate growth and success. Percentage Of Time 5 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required Minimum of 3 years of experience teaching reading or literacy in elementary grades (PreK-5th). Experience implementing, teaching with, or supporting teachers in the use of Louisiana High-Quality Instructional Materials ( HQIM ) (e.g., CKLA , Guidebooks, or equivalent Tier 1 curricula). Minimum Education Required Master’s Degree in Curriculum and Instruction with an emphasis on Reading, Literacy, or a closely related field. Minimum Licenses Required Louisiana Teacher Certification with Reading Specialist or Early Childhood/Elementary Reading endorsements. Other Minimum Requirements Ability to effectively teach reading-specific pedagogy grounded in the Science of Reading. Knowledge of current goals, state mandates, and reform practices in elementary reading and general educator preparation in Louisiana. Ability to promote candidate development of needed skills, knowledge, and attitudes expected of reading or literacy teachers. Ability to forecast and prioritize time to plan effectively. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Test(s) Required Preferred Education Preferred Experience Experience teaching reading or literacy in elementary grades (PreK-5th) Experience as a Master teacher and/or supervisor of preservice teachers. Active engagement with professional literacy and education organizations (e.g., International Literacy Association, Reading League, Council for Exceptional Children). Experience with teacher candidate assessment, accreditation (e.g., CAEP , TPI -US), and Louisiana Teacher Preparation Competencies. Experience teaching foundational or introductory undergraduate education courses. Experience with Canvas or other learning management systems ( LMS ) and Watermark or other assessment platforms for data entry and tracking. Preferred Licenses Other Preferred Requirements Physical Demands Employment Year Academic Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) 05/15/2027 Posting Date 10/06/2026 Closing Date 10/18/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants The anticipated start date for this position is January 13, 2027. Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10494 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Names and Contact Information for a Minimum of THREE References Copy of Transcript Optional Documents Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10516": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in K - 12 School Leadership",
      "description": "Nicholls State University Portal | Assistant Professor in K - 12 School Leadership Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor in K - 12 School Leadership Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The anticipated start date for this position is January 13, 2027. Special Instructions Nicholls State University adheres to the equal opportunity provisions of federal civil rights laws and regulations that are applicable to this agency. Therefore, no one will be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, national origin (Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964); sex (Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972); disability (Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; or age (Age Discrimination Act of 1975) in attaining educational goals and objectives and in the administration of personnel policies and procedures. Anyone with questions regarding this policy may contact Alison Hadaway, SHRM -CP, Director of Human Resources at 985-448-4041 / alison.hadaway@nicholls.edu / P.O. Box 2105, Thibodaux, LA 70310. For anyone needing ADA Accommodations, please contact Carolyn Kern, Director of Environmental Health & Safety at 985-448-4782 / carolyn.kern@nicholls.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor in K - 12 School Leadership Position Number 021322 Salary Range $55,233.00 Position Type Faculty Department Information Ending Effective Date of Temporary Employment Department Teacher Education Job Duties Responsibility / Duty Instruction & Course Delivery: Teach graduate courses related to school leadership standards in Louisiana across various modalities and undergraduate courses on a variety of topics as needed. (Minimum 9 hours per semester). Percentage Of Time 50 Responsibility / Duty Student Consultation & Office Hours: Maintain regular office hours to support candidates and collaborate with faculty colleagues. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Academic Advising & Residency Coordination: Serve as a faculty advisor to teacher candidates and as a university coordinator for candidates completing residency. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Departmental & Administrative Operations: Respond appropriately to administrative, departmental, and candidate needs; collaborate across university and departmental committees. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Accreditation, Data Collection & Reporting: Serve as a liaison with specialized professional associations. Work with Assessment and CAEP Coordinators to ensure seamless alignment of courses, rubrics, and key assignments with CAEP , state, and specialized professional standards, and assist with reporting and on-site visits. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Teaching, Scholarship & Service: Effectively engage in teaching, scholarship, and service (i.e., assessment, advisement, collaborative work in P-12 schools, etc.). Percentage Of Time 5 Responsibility / Duty Learning Environment & Engagement: Create and maintain a working environment conducive to excellence in teaching and learning. Percentage Of Time 5 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required Experience as a K-12 Educational School leader in a public school setting. Minimum Education Required Terminal degree or ABD in Educational Leadership (School Leadership) preferred. Enrollment in an Educational Leadership doctoral program accepted. Minimum Licenses Required Other Minimum Requirements Ability to promote candidate development of the skills, knowledge, and attitudes expected of graduates in the Educational Leadership Program. Mindful of goals and practices in the reform of leadership at all levels. Ability to forecast and prioritize time to plan effectively. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Test(s) Required Preferred Education Preferred Experience Experience as a K-12 Educational School leader in a public school setting. Experience with assessment and/or school improvement at the K-12 level. Experience with university accreditation related to graduate-level Educational Leadership. Pursues an advanced level of knowledge and pedagogy in Educational Leadership or related field (i.e., scholarship, leadership in professional associations, service, and/or publications). Experience with Canvas or other learning management systems ( LMS ) and Watermark or other assessment platforms for data entry and tracking. Preferred Licenses Other Preferred Requirements Physical Demands Employment Year Academic Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) 05/15/2027 Posting Date 10/06/2026 Closing Date 10/18/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants The anticipated start date for this position is January 13, 2027. Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10498 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Names and Contact Information for a Minimum of THREE References Copy of Transcript Optional Documents Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
