    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10515": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Curriculum and Instruction - Literacy",
      "description": "Nicholls State University Portal | Assistant Professor in Curriculum and Instruction - Literacy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor in Curriculum and Instruction - Literacy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The anticipated start date for this position is January 13, 2027. Special Instructions Nicholls State University adheres to the equal opportunity provisions of federal civil rights laws and regulations that are applicable to this agency. Therefore, no one will be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, national origin (Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964); sex (Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972); disability (Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; or age (Age Discrimination Act of 1975) in attaining educational goals and objectives and in the administration of personnel policies and procedures. Anyone with questions regarding this policy may contact Alison Hadaway, SHRM -CP, Director of Human Resources at 985-448-4041 / alison.hadaway@nicholls.edu / P.O. Box 2105, Thibodaux, LA 70310. For anyone needing ADA Accommodations, please contact Carolyn Kern, Director of Environmental Health & Safety at 985-448-4782 / carolyn.kern@nicholls.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor in Curriculum and Instruction - Literacy Position Number 500020 Salary Range $55,233.00 Position Type Faculty Department Information Ending Effective Date of Temporary Employment Department Teacher Education Job Duties Responsibility / Duty Instruction & Course Delivery: Teach graduate and undergraduate courses in PreK-5 reading pedagogy, diagnostic assessment, and structured literacy aligned with the Science of Reading and Louisiana HQIM (minimum 9 credit hours per semester or equivalent). Percentage Of Time 50 Responsibility / Duty Accreditation, Assessment & State Compliance: Serve as a liaison with specialized professional associations. Work with Assessment and CAEP Coordinators to ensure seamless alignment of courses, rubrics, and key assignments with CAEP , state, and specialized professional standards, and assist with reporting and on-site visits. Collaborate with the Department Head to update courses, syllabi, and degree pathways to reflect current Science of Reading research and state-adopted HQIM in undergraduate and graduate programs. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Departmental & Administrative Operations: Respond appropriately to administrative, departmental, and candidate needs; collaborate across university and departmental committees. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Academic Advising & Student Coordination: Serve as a faculty advisor and university coordinator for teacher candidates completing clinical experiences or program milestones. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Student Consultation & Office Hours: Maintain regular, scheduled office hours to ensure accessibility to candidates, colleagues, and community partners. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Scholarship & Continuous Professional Growth: Maintain an active research agenda and continuously pursue advanced knowledge in early childhood/elementary reading, structured literacy, PK-5 pedagogy, and related publications. Percentage Of Time 5 Responsibility / Duty P-12 Collaboration & Service: Actively engage in departmental, university, and community service, including program evaluation and collaborative literacy partnerships with PK-12 schools. Percentage Of Time 5 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required Minimum of 3 years of experience teaching reading or literacy in elementary grades (PreK-5th). Experience implementing, teaching with, or supporting teachers in the use of Louisiana High-Quality Instructional Materials ( HQIM ) (e.g., CKLA , Guidebooks, or equivalent Tier 1 curricula). Minimum Education Required Doctoral Degree in Curriculum and Instruction with an emphasis on Reading or Literacy or a closely related field. ABD Considered. Minimum Licenses Required Louisiana Teacher Certification with Reading Specialist or Early Childhood/Elementary Reading endorsements. Other Minimum Requirements Trained in the Science of Reading. Ability to promote candidates’ development of the skills, knowledge, and dispositions required of modern PreK-5 literacy educators. Mindful of state and national goals and evidence-based practices in the reform of early and elementary reading education. Strong organizational skills with the ability to forecast, prioritize, and manage time effectively. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Test(s) Required Preferred Education Preferred Experience Experience teaching reading/literacy in elementary (grades 1-5). Experience teaching reading in Pre-Kindergarten, Kindergarten, or Middle School grades (6-8) considered. Experience as a Master Teacher, Literacy Coach, or supervisor of preservice or in-service teachers. Experience with assessment, accreditation, and school improvement processes at the university or P-12 level. Familiarity with the International Literacy Association ( ILA ), International Dyslexia Association ( IDA ), Council for the Accreditation of Educator Preparation ( CAEP ), Louisiana Teacher Preparation Competencies, and/or state review entities. Active engagement in scholarship, leadership, service, or publication related to early/elementary literacy development or structured literacy implementation. Experience using higher education or PK-12 student success and assessment platforms (e.g., Canvas, Watermark). Preferred Licenses Other Preferred Requirements Physical Demands Employment Year Academic Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) 05/15/2027 Posting Date 10/06/2026 Closing Date 10/18/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants The anticipated start date for this position is January 13, 2027. Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10496 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Names and Contact Information for a Minimum of THREE References Copy of Transcript Optional Documents Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
