    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10485": {
      "title": "Instructor or Assistant Professor of Civil Engineering",
      "description": "Nicholls State University Portal | Instructor or Assistant Professor of Civil Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Instructor or Assistant Professor of Civil Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Special Instructions Nicholls State University adheres to the equal opportunity provisions of federal civil rights laws and regulations that are applicable to this agency. Therefore, no one will be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, national origin (Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964); sex (Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972); disability (Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; or age (Age Discrimination Act of 1975) in attaining educational goals and objectives and in the administration of personnel policies and procedures. Anyone with questions regarding this policy may contact Alison Hadaway, SHRM -CP, Director of Human Resources at 985-448-4041 / alison.hadaway@nicholls.edu / P.O. Box 2105, Thibodaux, LA 70310. For anyone needing ADA Accommodations, please contact Carolyn Kern, Director of Environmental Health & Safety at 985-448-4782 / carolyn.kern@nicholls.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Instructor or Assistant Professor of Civil Engineering Position Number 500257 Salary Range $75,000-$85,000 Position Type Faculty Department Information Ending Effective Date of Temporary Employment Department Wm. Clifford Smith School of Engineering Job Duties Responsibility / Duty Providing high-quality teaching in courses produced by the School as assigned by the Director and based on department and university needs, including holding requisite office hours and abiding by all faculty responsibilities as defined by University Policy and Procedure. Percentage Of Time 70 Responsibility / Duty Providing service to the department, college, university, and profession including but not limited to student advising, committee work, recruiting, and volunteer activity. The person in this position will be expected to (1) advise students in concentration curricula related to the faculty member’s background; (2) serve on departmental committees as assigned; (3) provide committee and other service to the School, College and University; and (4) serve as volunteer and department and university representatives on extracurricular and sometimes after-hours events. The person in this position is expected to perform teaching and mentoring duties with particular focus on student access, progress, and success, as well as engage in collegial and collaborative activities with other university faculty. Percentage Of Time 15 Responsibility / Duty Conducting scientific research and scholarship in teaching and learning in the field, which shall include successful grantsmanship, mentorship of students, service on undergraduate (Honors) and graduate student thesis committees, participating in professional development opportunities, presenting research findings at professional meetings and to the general public, and publishing scholarly articles in scientific journals. Percentage Of Time 15 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required Demonstrated ability to communicate complex technical concepts effectively to a diverse student body. Proficiency in C++ and or python programming, AutoCAD Civil 3D for engineering applications and numerical analysis . Minimum Education Required A Master of Science (M.S.) in Civil Engineering, Engineering Technology, or a closely related engineering field from an accredited institution. Minimum Licenses Required Other Minimum Requirements Test(s) Required Preferred Education A Ph.D. in Civil Engineering or Engineering Technology is strongly preferred. Preferred Experience Previous teaching experience at the collegiate level or significant industrial experience in civil design or technical manufacturing. Experience or ability to teach core courses in core engineering sciences (statics, mechanics, materials), civil engineering specialties (fluids, structures. geotechnical, hydrological), or engineering design is preferred. Experience in engineering course development. · Experience with ABET accreditation. Proficiency with industry-standard software such as, Revit, SolidWorks, or specialized engineering analysis tools. Preferred Licenses Professional Engineering (P.E.) licensure or the ability to obtain licensure in the state of Louisiana. Other Preferred Requirements Physical Demands Employment Year Academic Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) 05/15/2027 Posting Date 06/23/2026 Closing Date 10/31/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/9990 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Names and Contact Information for a Minimum of THREE References Copy of Transcript Optional Documents Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
